WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.133 --> 00:00:17.244
As Jill Ashley hurried off, Henry looked at his friends.

2
00:00:17.264 --> 00:00:21.847
"We'll have to work fast if we want to solve this mystery," he said.

3
00:00:21.867 --> 00:00:26.231
"The ride will probably start up again after those new tires get here."

4
00:00:26.251 --> 00:00:29.914
"Then let's not waste any time," Cole said.

5
00:00:29.934 --> 00:00:31.856
"Who should we question next?"

6
00:00:32.880 --> 00:00:34.020
"How about William?"

7
00:00:34.440 --> 00:00:37.821
Maggie pointed to the new boy, who was kneeling by his front tire.

8
00:00:37.841 --> 00:00:40.082
"He's one of our suspects.

9
00:00:40.762 --> 00:00:42.063
And he's right over there."

10
00:00:42.963 --> 00:00:45.343
The Lemonade Detectives walked over to William.

11
00:00:45.363 --> 00:00:47.844
"Hi," Henry greeted him.

12
00:00:47.864 --> 00:00:50.285
"Did your tire get slashed?"

13
00:00:51.225 --> 00:00:53.406
"Yes!" William scowled.

14
00:00:53.426 --> 00:00:55.566
"And it was really expensive."

15
00:00:56.806 --> 00:00:57.767
Just then Ms.

16
00:00:57.807 --> 00:00:59.747
Hernandez called for everyone’s attention.

17
00:00:59.767 --> 00:01:03.092
"I spoke to Belltown Bikes," she announced.

18
00:01:03.112 --> 00:01:07.095
"They'll be here in about 15 minutes with replacement tires.

19
00:01:08.095 --> 00:01:12.537
The ride will continue once everyone's bike is fixed, so please be patient."

20
00:01:13.438 --> 00:01:15.859
"That doesn't give us much time," said Cole.

21
00:01:16.500 --> 00:01:17.280
Henry nodded.

22
00:01:18.140 --> 00:01:22.403
He turned to ask William another question, but the boy had disappeared while Ms.

23
00:01:22.443 --> 00:01:23.623
Hernandez was talking.

24
00:01:23.643 --> 00:01:26.525
"That's odd," Henry thought.

25
00:01:27.445 --> 00:01:28.686
Maggie had noticed too.

26
00:01:28.706 --> 00:01:31.147
"Hey, where did William go?"

27
00:01:31.608 --> 00:01:32.168
she asked.

28
00:01:33.108 --> 00:01:33.888
Cole shrugged.

29
00:01:33.908 --> 00:01:35.269
"Never mind.

30
00:01:35.929 --> 00:01:37.729
We can't waste time looking for him now."

31
00:01:38.750 --> 00:01:40.170
"Right," Henry agreed.

32
00:01:40.190 --> 00:01:43.231
"Let's split up so we can interview more people.

33
00:01:44.131 --> 00:01:48.953
Try to find out who left the picnic area, how long they were gone, and who was with

34
00:01:49.013 --> 00:01:52.094
them. We'll meet back here in 15 minutes."

35
00:01:53.374 --> 00:01:57.735
His friends nodded and hurried off, and Henry looked around.

36
00:01:58.776 --> 00:02:00.076
Who should he talk to first?

37
00:02:01.344 --> 00:02:03.245
He saw Tiny and his friends nearby.

38
00:02:03.265 --> 00:02:06.505
"Hi, Henry," Tiny greeted him.

39
00:02:07.086 --> 00:02:08.166
"How are your tires?"

40
00:02:08.186 --> 00:02:10.807
"They're fine," Henry said.

41
00:02:10.827 --> 00:02:12.347
"What about yours?"

42
00:02:13.347 --> 00:02:14.268
Tiny sighed.

43
00:02:14.988 --> 00:02:20.709
"I got my front and back tires slashed," he said, pointing to his bike.

44
00:02:20.729 --> 00:02:24.090
"Hey, you're a detective, right?

45
00:02:24.911 --> 00:02:26.851
Maybe you can figure out who did this!"

46
00:02:26.871 --> 00:02:29.772
"I'm trying," Henry said.

47
00:02:30.640 --> 00:02:33.982
"I want to figure out who left the picnic area while we were all there."

48
00:02:34.002 --> 00:02:35.603
"Not us."

49
00:02:36.023 --> 00:02:37.384
Tiny glanced at his friends.

50
00:02:37.404 --> 00:02:41.526
"But some of the girls we were sitting with went to the restroom."

51
00:02:41.546 --> 00:02:43.907
"Did they all walk there together?"

52
00:02:44.227 --> 00:02:45.008
Henry asked.

53
00:02:46.048 --> 00:02:47.349
One of Tiny's friends laughed.

54
00:02:47.369 --> 00:02:48.750
"Of course!

55
00:02:49.410 --> 00:02:51.471
Girls always go to the bathroom together."

56
00:02:51.491 --> 00:02:54.553
"Yeah," Tiny agreed with a grin.

57
00:02:55.273 --> 00:02:57.675
"That way they can talk about us boys!"

58
00:02:58.835 --> 00:02:59.676
Henry smiled.

59
00:03:00.332 --> 00:03:03.854
"Did you notice anyone else disappearing for a long time?"

60
00:03:03.874 --> 00:03:06.296
"No." Tiny shrugged.

61
00:03:06.316 --> 00:03:09.538
"Wait, I did," the other friend said.

62
00:03:09.558 --> 00:03:12.240
"It was that weird guy with the dark glasses."

63
00:03:12.260 --> 00:03:15.882
"You're right," said Tiny's friend with the blond hair.

64
00:03:15.902 --> 00:03:17.744
"He's hard to miss!

65
00:03:18.444 --> 00:03:21.186
I think that kid from Valley High left for a while too."

66
00:03:22.147 --> 00:03:23.147
He rolled his eyes.

67
00:03:23.167 --> 00:03:25.149
"I don't like him at all."

68
00:03:26.109 --> 00:03:27.690
Just then Daisy walked over.

69
00:03:27.710 --> 00:03:29.952
"Hi, Henry," she said.

70
00:03:30.796 --> 00:03:34.998
"Are The Lemonade Detectives trying to solve the case of the slashed tires?"

71
00:03:35.018 --> 00:03:37.380
"Yes," Henry said.

72
00:03:37.400 --> 00:03:39.901
"I just thought of something.

73
00:03:40.641 --> 00:03:43.323
What if it wasn't someone from the ride at all?"

74
00:03:43.643 --> 00:03:44.323
Tiny said.

75
00:03:44.343 --> 00:03:46.745
"This is a public park.

76
00:03:47.485 --> 00:03:48.746
It could have been anyone."

77
00:03:49.646 --> 00:03:50.787
Daisy shook her head.

78
00:03:50.807 --> 00:03:56.670
"Who would follow us all the way out here just to slash our tires?

79
00:03:57.871 --> 00:04:00.192
Besides I bet I know who did it."

80
00:04:01.068 --> 00:04:02.509
"Who?" Henry asked.

81
00:04:02.529 --> 00:04:06.531
"That guy with the sunglasses," Daisy said.

82
00:04:06.551 --> 00:04:09.053
"Nobody knows who he is.

83
00:04:09.713 --> 00:04:13.475
Plus, he was only at the picnic area for a few minutes."

84
00:04:14.496 --> 00:04:16.357
Henry saw a flash of red and gold.

85
00:04:17.197 --> 00:04:21.600
When he looked over, he saw the boy from Valley High School hurrying toward the restrooms.

86
00:04:22.620 --> 00:04:26.182
The other student from Valley High School, Tina, was following him.

87
00:04:26.202 --> 00:04:28.223
"What about Tina?"

88
00:04:28.524 --> 00:04:29.064
he asked.

89
00:04:29.752 --> 00:04:32.213
"Did anyone notice if she left the picnic area?"

90
00:04:33.033 --> 00:04:33.813
Daisy nodded.

91
00:04:33.833 --> 00:04:36.514
"I think I saw her leave for a while.

92
00:04:37.294 --> 00:04:38.274
She’s really nice.

93
00:04:38.334 --> 00:04:39.615
Is she a suspect?"

94
00:04:39.635 --> 00:04:42.535
"I'm not sure yet," Henry said.

95
00:04:42.555 --> 00:04:44.876
"I need to get all the facts first."

96
00:04:48.857 --> 00:04:51.898
He spent the next few minutes questioning several other people.

97
00:04:55.999 --> 00:04:58.760
Then it was time to meet the other Lemonade Detectives.

98
00:04:59.796 --> 00:05:00.837
"What did you find out?"

99
00:05:01.217 --> 00:05:03.499
Henry asked when the three of them were together again.

100
00:05:03.519 --> 00:05:09.263
"Almost everyone saw that guy with the sunglasses leave the picnic area," Maggie said.

101
00:05:09.283 --> 00:05:14.527
"A few people noticed that William left too, but nobody saw him come back."

102
00:05:15.588 --> 00:05:17.149
"Hmm said Henry.

103
00:05:17.169 --> 00:05:20.491
"I found out the same thing," said Cole.

104
00:05:20.511 --> 00:05:26.716
"I also found out that Joey and Tina, the two kids from Valley High, left for a while.

105
00:05:27.748 --> 00:05:31.111
What if they planned this prank to make Belltown look bad?"

106
00:05:32.212 --> 00:05:34.414
"Maybe we should talk to them," Henry said.

107
00:05:39.358 --> 00:05:43.041
He and his friends found Joey and Tina standing outside the restrooms.

108
00:05:43.942 --> 00:05:47.124
But they weren't laughing over the prank or plotting more trouble.

109
00:05:48.085 --> 00:05:50.327
Tina looked angry as she glared at Joey.

110
00:05:50.347 --> 00:05:54.731
"I know you slashed those tires, and you'd better confess!"

111
00:05:55.171 --> 00:05:55.872
she yelled at him.

112
00:05:56.857 --> 00:05:58.910
"You're making our school look bad!"
